>> title: Corn Tortillas
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: corn, masa, mexican, griddle, vegan
>> counters: Taquería, Panadería
>> aka: tortillas de maíz, tortilla taquera
>> servings: 24
>> time: 12 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — cal is caustic and the steep cannot be restarted: too short and the hulls will not rub off, too long and the corn grinds to mush
>> step.2: simmer 20 min, then steep 8 hr
>> step.3: drain, rub off the hulls

Bring @dried field corn{1%lb}(450 g; dent or cacahuazintle), @water{2%qt}(2 L), and @cal{2%tsp}(4.5 g; slaked lime, 1% of the corn's weight) to a boil.

Simmer @&(~1)corn{} ~{20%min}, then steep off the heat ~{8%hr}.

Drain @&(~1)nixtamal{} and rub off the loosened hulls under running water.

Grind @&(~1)nixtamal{} to a smooth stiff masa with @fine sea salt{1%tsp}(5 g).

Knead @&(~1)masa{} with @warm water{1/4%cup}(60 mL).

Press @&(~1)masa{} into 5-in rounds and cook on a dry #comal{} ~{1%min} per side.
